  greetings:
  - Klein. You're still here.
  - Go home, Klein. ...Oh. Right. The letter.
  aboutSelf: Thirty-one years on this desk. I know every voice in the county by its second word. The sheriff's, the drunks', and the ones that call and don't say anything.
  aboutTown: 'Semblance? Two hours north, past Barlow. Farm town: one church, one diner, one road through it. In thirty-one years this office has never had a call from there. Not a stolen truck. Not a drunk. Nothing at all.'
  seenAnythingStrange: Teo's dog got out again. Half blind, that animal, and she goes and sits in the archive facing the wall, like she's waiting for somebody to come through it.
  foundersDay: 
  gossip:
  - title: About Teodoro Baptiste
    response: Teo? Clocked out at ten, same as always. Thursdays he's off anyway, so I don't know why he was in at all.
